details:
(a) increase in the total length of National Highways in the State of Haryana during the last five years, district-wise details thereof;
(b) whether Government has any proposal to expand the National Highway network in Haryana through four/six-laning of National Highways, Greenfield Corridors, Ring Roads and Bypass projects, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government has prepared any long-term action plan to enhance the overall route density and carrying capacity of National Highways in Haryana in view of the increasing industrial, agricultural and freight traffic in the State, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the quantum of new capacity installed under solar energy, rooftop solar, bio-energy, and other renewable energy projects during the past two years in Haryana and the details thereof, district-wise; 
(b) whether Government has any specific scheme or proposal to provide financial assistance to promote green hydrogen, solar parks and agricultural solar energy projects in the State, if so, the details thereof; and 
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of the renewable energy sector in the State on employment generation, industrial investment and reduction of carbon emissions, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of cases taken up and disposed of through e-Lok Adalats during the last three years, State-wise and year wise;
(b) the total amount of monetary settlement arrived through e-Lok Adalats during the said period;
(c) the States/Union Territories where e-Lok Adalats have been introduced or expanded during the said period; and
(d) the further steps proposed to expand this initiative across the country?

(a) whether Government has made any improvements to NCS portal to make it more user-friendly and accessible for job seekers and if so, the details of all such improvements;
(b) the number of Memorandums of Understanding (MoUs) signed with private and Government partners to enhance the service offerings of NCS;
(c) the number of Model Career Centres (MCCs) operational in the country and the role being played by them in promoting the use of NCS portal; and
(d) whether all State employment exchanges/State career services have been digitized and integrated with NCS portal?

(a) the mission-wise status of deployment of Global Passport Seva Programme (GPSP V2.0) across Indian Embassies and Consulates;
(b) the number of overseas Indian nationals served through this programme, so far, country-wise;
(c) the specific technical or administrative challenges faced in extending this service to all diplomatic missions; and 
(d) the countries identified for extension of the programme in the near future and the timeline proposed for the same?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment of ecological outcomes and environmental benefits achieved under the Green Credit Programme since its implementation, and if so, the findings thereof;
(b) whether Government has developed a framework for monitoring, verification and long-term ecological assessment of activities undertaken under the Programme;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government proposes to expand the scope of the Programme beyond tree plantation and water conservation to cover other environmental sectors; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the quantitative improvement recorded in the Sex Ratio at Birth and the Gross Enrolment Ratio of girls in school education since the launch of the ‘Beti Bachao Beti Padhao’ initiative;
(b) the strategic framework adopted to ensure convergence of education and health interventions aimed at improving the retention of girls in secondary and higher education;
(c) whether community mobilisation campaigns and behaviour modification communication strategies are being intensified in districts with poor Child Sex Ratio; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of implementation regarding the five University Townships envisioned in the Union Budget 2026-27 near prominent industrial and logistics hubs;
(b) the framework through which these hubs seek to integrate academic institutions, research facilities and centres for skill development to enhance industry-academia synergy;
(c) the current status of the constitution of the High-Powered Standing Committee on Education to Employment and Enterprise and its core mandates;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the strategic initiatives undertaken to synchronise higher education to align with labour-market needs and improve the industry-readiness of graduates?

(a) the current operational status of the newly established National Multi-State Cooperative Societies (MSCS) dedicated to exports, organic products and seed production;
(b) the mechanisms adopted for distribution of surplus generated by these societies among their member cooperative societies in accordance with their bye-laws;
(c) whether Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) are being incorporated as the grassroots collection and service points for these national apex organisations; 
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the specific initiatives implemented to facilitate organic certification and grant small and marginal farmers access to high-value international export markets?

(a) the progress achieved under the "Sahakar se Samriddhi" vision in setting up new multipurpose Primary Agriculture Cooperative Credit Societies (PACS), dairy and fishery cooperative societies in previously unserved Gram Panchayats;
(b) whether the adoption of Model Bye-Laws has successfully empowered primary societies to expand their operational scope into diverse service-delivery domains;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the specific strategies formulated to bridge regional disparities and revitalise the cooperative movement in States where its presence is relatively low?

(a) the status and timeline of finalisation and notification of the draft Floating Solar PV (FSPV) Potential Assessment Report and the draft Floating Solar Policy prepared by the National Institute of Solar Energy (NISE) and IIT Roorkee;
(b) the total floating solar potential identified across water bodies in the country under this assessment, State/UT-wise;
(c) whether the draft policy proposes a single-window clearance mechanism for floating solar projects involving multiple State departments and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the targets, if any, fixed for FSPV capacity addition by 2030?

(a) whether Small Industries Development Bank of India (SIDBI) has undertaken major initiatives during the last five years to improve the flow of credit to Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) across the country;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has operationalised the Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme (ECLGS) 5.0;
(d) if so, the details of additional credit flow targeted thereunder, including guarantee coverage for MSMEs and support to the aviation sector; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the total number of accounts opened under Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) till date;
(b) the State/UT-wise number of PMJDY Account holders as of May 2026;
(c) whether any facilities are being provided to the PMJDY Account holders, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether there are any minimum balance charges for the PMJDY Account holders, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the number of women Jan Dhan Account holders?

(a) whether it is a fact that the total quantity of Wheat and Rice held in the Central Pool as on 1st April, 2026 exceeded the prescribed buffer norms;
(b) whether the quantum of wheat procurement achieved during the Rabi Marketing Season 2026–27 is higher as compared to the previous season;
(c) whether Government has data on the number of farmers who benefited through Minimum Support Price (MSP) operations during the Rabi Marketing Season 2026–27;
(d) whether Government has taken steps to ensure efficient utilisation of surplus foodgrain stocks so as to optimise storage costs; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) total amount of delay compensation owed to MGNREGA workers as on the date of repeal (June 30, 2026) that remains unpaid, State-wise, including Bihar;
(b) the number of States/UTs that had completed the transition of their MIS, Aadhaar-seeding and Fund Transfer Order systems to the VB-G RAM G framework by the effective date of July 1, 2026;
(c) whether any assessment has been made of pending or stalled works under the erstwhile MGNREGA that require re-approval or re-classification under the new Act's four thematic work categories; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of cold storage and integrated cold chain projects sanctioned and completed so far;
(b) the steps taken to reduce post-harvest losses of perishable agricultural produce through cold chain and preservation infrastructure; and
(c) whether the Ministry maintains the State-wise details of the financial assistance actually disbursed to Farmer Producer Organisations (FPOs) for value addition under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana (PMKSY) and the Pradhan Mantri Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) Scheme during the last three years, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether there is an action plan to implement digital legal aid services and the 'Nyaya Setu' chatbot at the district and sub-divisional levels in Haryana under Designing Innovative Solutions for Holistic Access to Justice (DISHA) 2.0 and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has any specific scheme to expand 'VIDHI-Sanjeevani' and other digital legal aid services for rural and vulnerable sections in the State and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether any financial assistance has been sanctioned to the State under DISHA 2.0 and the improvement in access to justice and the disposal of pending cases expected in the State as a result thereof?

(a) district-wise details of National Highway projects sanctioned, under construction and completed in the State of Haryana during the last five years, along with the total expenditure incurred thereon;
(b) whether Government has any proposal to develop new National Highways, bypasses, flyovers and expressways to ease traffic congestion in Karnal, Panipat, Sonepat, Yamunanagar and other industrial and agricultural areas of Haryana, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government has any specific action plan for the development of the Delhi–Panipat–Karnal–Yamunanagar–Paonta Sahib Economic Corridor and for providing better National Highway connectivity to the major industrial, agricultural and logistics hubs of Haryana, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the overall progress achieved under the 'PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana' (PMSGMBY) up to May 2026, including the number of rooftop solar installations completed and the number of households benefited thereunder;
(b) the details of the Central Financial Assistance released under the scheme, along with the average time taken for processing and disbursing subsidy claims;
(c) the measures taken to address implementation challenges under the scheme, particularly with regard to delays in installation in low-performing States, DISCOM readiness and grid connectivity; and
(d) the expected contribution of the Scheme towards achieving the target of one crore rooftop solar households and its impact on distributed renewable energy generation and the reduction of carbon emissions?

(a) whether any research project or financial assistance has been sanctioned to AYUSH institutions, universities and research centres in Haryana under the AYURGYAN Scheme and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has any proposal to establish an All India Institute of Ayurveda (AIIA) or a Centre of Excellence in Haryana to strengthen Ayurveda research, education and integrated healthcare services and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government has formulated any special action plan to expand the integrated healthcare model of AYUSH and modern medicine and promote Ayurveda-based research and treatment facilities in Haryana and if so, the details thereof?

(a) name of the cities in Haryana covered under AMRUT 2.0, and the amount of central assistance released to the State so far;
(b) whether Government has evaluated the progress regarding drinking water supply, sewerage, water recycling, rainwater harvesting and the rejuvenation of urban water bodies in the cities of Haryana approved under AMRUT 2.0, if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has any proposal to provide additional financial assistance for 24×7 drinking water supply, functional water tap connections and the conservation of urban lakes and water bodies in Haryana's cities, specifically Panipat, Karnal, Sonipat, Gurugram and Faridabad; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of new rural roads constructed and upgraded in Haryana during the year 2025–26, and the number of habitations that were provided all-weather road connectivity under Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY);
(b) whether Government has any proposal under PMGSY-IV to provide better road connectivity to the remaining eligible villages, agricultural markets, and rural industrial areas in Haryana, if so, the details thereof; and 
(c) the amount of central assistance approved for road construction, upgradation, and maintenance under PMGSY in Haryana during the year 2026–27 and the districts that have been given priority?

(a) the progress made in reducing air pollution in the cities of Haryana, especially Gurugram, Faridabad, Panipat, Sonipat and Yamunanagar under the National Clean Air Programme (NCAP) and the amount of central assistance provided therefor;
(b) the details of specific action plan for controlling pollution, rejuvenating, and conserving wetlands of Yamuna and other major rivers in Haryana; and
(c) the details of special arrangements made through the PARIVESH portal, to make the process of environmental clearances more transparent and faster in Haryana and to take effective action against illegal mining and polluting activities?

(a) the number of projects approved and the amount of financial assistance sanctioned, so far, for universities, research institutions, startups and industries in Haryana under ANRF;
(b) whether Government has any specific scheme to promote research related to deep-tech, artificial intelligence (AI), biotechnology, agritech and manufacturing innovation in Haryana and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government proposes to establish any Centre of Excellence under ANRF to foster research and innovation collaboration among academic institutions, industries and startups in Haryana, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of National High-Speed Corridor and Greenfield Expressway projects approved, under construction and completed in Haryana and the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has any specific action plan to complete pending National Highway and Expressway projects in Haryana within the stipulated timeframe and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether there is any proposal under consideration by Government to develop new High-Speed Corridors or Expressways to improve connectivity for the industrial, agricultural and logistics sectors in Haryana and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the preparations for the Census-2027 in Haryana including house listing, the housing census and digital data collection have commenced, if so, the current status thereof;
(b) whether the arrangements for self-enumeration facilities, digital devices and training of Census personnel for Census 2027 in Haryana have been completed, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the financial assistance released by the Central Government to Haryana so far for preparations for Census-2027 and the details of the heads under which the same is being utilised?

(a) the number of eligible families and beneficiaries in Haryana received benefits under the Ayushman Bharat–Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) so far and the details thereof, district-wise;
(b) whether Government has any proposal to provide Ayushman cards to all eligible families in Haryana and to increase the number of Ayushman Arogya Mandirs and empanelled hospitals, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether any specific action plan has been prepared in Haryana for the widespread use of ABHA IDs and the complete integration of Government and private hospitals under the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the key features of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) 2.0 and the major changes that have been made in it as compared to the previous phase of the Mission;
(b) the implementation framework and funding pattern under the Mission;
(c) the reforms proposed to strengthen source sustainability, operation and maintenance of rural water supply systems and community participation;
(d) the State-wise funds allocated and released under JJM 2.0 during the year 2026-27; and
(e) the timeline and targets for achieving universal and sustainable rural household tap water supply under the Mission?

(a) the current status of metro rail projects sanctioned and under implementation across the country as of June 2026, along with the details of project-wise physical progress;
(b) the details of the financial assistance provided by the Central Government to States and implementing agencies for metro rail expansion;
(c) whether new cities or corridors have been approved under the ongoing metro rail expansion proposals in the State of Haryana;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the impact of the expansion of metro rail in the State of Haryana on urban mobility, congestion reduction, and last-mile connectivity?
